cls-turn-not-approved = Content was not approved for sending to the selected model.
cls-turn-blocked = Content policy prevents sending this request to the selected model. Remove the content the policy names, or ask an administrator which data may be used here.
cls-turn-model-not-cleared = This conversation is classified { $level }; the selected model is not cleared for it. Choose a model that is cleared for that level.
cls-tool-hidden = { $tool } is not available in this conversation, which is classified { $level }; the tool is not cleared for that level. Use another tool, or continue in a new conversation.
cls-gate-blocked = { $tool } was not called: its arguments contain data of class { $classes }, which the tool is not cleared for. Remove that data from the arguments or use another tool.
cls-gate-unavailable = { $tool } was not called: the model that checks its arguments could not be reached, so nothing leaves the conversation unchecked. Retry later or ask an administrator to check the detector model.
cls-detector-unavailable = The message was not sent: the model that checks it for classified content could not be reached, so nothing goes to a model unchecked. Retry later or ask an administrator to check the detector model.

# Template texts: the administrator's language; applied, they become the scheme's own data.
cls-tpl-iso-name = ISO/IEC 27001 (four levels)
cls-tpl-iso-description = Public, internal, confidential and strictly confidential: the scheme most ISO 27001 information classification policies use.
cls-tpl-iso-level-public-name = Public
cls-tpl-iso-level-public-description = May be shared with anyone.
cls-tpl-iso-level-internal-name = Internal
cls-tpl-iso-level-internal-description = For staff and trusted partners; not for the public.
cls-tpl-iso-level-confidential-name = Confidential
cls-tpl-iso-level-confidential-description = Limited to those who need it; disclosure harms the business.
cls-tpl-iso-level-strictly_confidential-name = Strictly confidential
cls-tpl-iso-level-strictly_confidential-description = A named circle only; disclosure causes severe damage.
cls-tpl-tisax-name = TISAX / VDA ISA
cls-tpl-tisax-description = The four protection classes of the VDA information security assessment: public, internal, confidential and strictly confidential, with the German stamps automotive documents carry.
cls-tpl-tisax-level-public-name = Public
cls-tpl-tisax-level-public-description = Öffentlich: may be published.
cls-tpl-tisax-level-internal-name = Internal
cls-tpl-tisax-level-internal-description = Intern: for employees and contractors bound by agreement.
cls-tpl-tisax-level-confidential-name = Confidential
cls-tpl-tisax-level-confidential-description = Vertraulich: a defined group of recipients.
cls-tpl-tisax-level-strictly_confidential-name = Strictly confidential
cls-tpl-tisax-level-strictly_confidential-description = Streng vertraulich: named recipients only.
cls-tpl-bsi-name = BSI IT-Grundschutz protection requirement
cls-tpl-bsi-description = The three protection requirement categories of BSI IT-Grundschutz: normal, high and very high.
cls-tpl-bsi-level-normal-name = Normal
cls-tpl-bsi-level-normal-description = Schutzbedarf normal: damage is limited and manageable.
cls-tpl-bsi-level-high-name = High
cls-tpl-bsi-level-high-description = Schutzbedarf hoch: damage can be considerable.
cls-tpl-bsi-level-very_high-name = Very high
cls-tpl-bsi-level-very_high-description = Schutzbedarf sehr hoch: damage can threaten the existence of the organisation.
cls-tpl-tlp-name = TLP 2.0 (Traffic Light Protocol)
cls-tpl-tlp-description = The five sharing labels of FIRST's Traffic Light Protocol 2.0: clear, green, amber, amber+strict and red.
cls-tpl-tlp-level-clear-name = TLP:CLEAR
cls-tpl-tlp-level-clear-description = No limit on disclosure.
cls-tpl-tlp-level-green-name = TLP:GREEN
cls-tpl-tlp-level-green-description = The community, not the public.
cls-tpl-tlp-level-amber-name = TLP:AMBER
cls-tpl-tlp-level-amber-description = The organisation and the clients that need it.
cls-tpl-tlp-level-amber_strict-name = TLP:AMBER+STRICT
cls-tpl-tlp-level-amber_strict-description = The organisation only.
cls-tpl-tlp-level-red-name = TLP:RED
cls-tpl-tlp-level-red-description = Named recipients only; no further sharing.
cls-class-personal_data-name = Personal data
cls-class-personal_data-description = Information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person (GDPR Art. 4).
cls-class-special_categories-name = Special categories of personal data
cls-class-special_categories-description = Health, biometric, genetic, religious, political, trade-union, sexual-orientation or ethnic-origin data about a person (GDPR Art. 9).
cls-class-trade_secrets-name = Trade secrets and NDA-covered content
cls-class-trade_secrets-description = Information the company protects as a secret or has agreed to keep confidential.
cls-class-payment_data-name = Payment data
cls-class-payment_data-description = Bank account and payment card numbers.
cls-class-tax_id-name = Tax identification number
cls-class-tax_id-description = The German personal tax identification number (Steuer-ID).
cls-class-credentials-name = Credentials and keys
cls-class-credentials-description = Passwords, API keys, tokens and private keys.
cls-model-group-system-one = System One (recommended)
cls-model-group-chat = Chat models (fallback)
cls-model-chat-warning = A chat model is slower, costs a model call per message and is less robust against manipulated content than System One.
cls-model-none-available = No detector model is set up. Add a System One or chat model on the models page.
cls-model-none-available-link = Open the models page
